and the public information officer with  the north Las Vegas Police Department  today we are going over an incident that  occurred on the 5000 block of North  Scott Robinson  right now is a brief recap of the  information of what has been put out  already  on December 11 2022 at about 9 16 PM  officers responded to the area of the  5000 block of North Scott Robinson to a  report of a single vehicle traffic  collision  arriving officers located a vehicle that  had struck a tree medical personnel were  called to the scene a juvenile believed  to be around toddler age was pronounced  deceased on scene three others two  adults and one juvenile were transported  to UMC Hospital  the driver of the van is a female  believed to be in her 20s the second  adult passenger is a female but her age  remains unknown at this time  the second juvenile is believed to be  toddler age as well and was later  pronounced deceased at UMC Hospital  two adults remain in serious condition  nlvpd Traffic Division and CSI were  called to the scene  the preliminary investigation revealed  the following  a silver Honda was traveling Northbound  on Scott Robinson from Lone Mountain  the Honda failed to maintain Lane and  sideswiped trees a light pole a wall and  then struck a large palm tree head-on  two juveniles were not wearing  age-appropriate child safety restraints  resulting in the toddler the initial  toddler being decapitated  and the other later succumbing to his  injuries her injuries  speed and impairment are believed to be  factors at this time  the identification of the victims as  well as cause and manner of death will  be released by The Clark County  coroner's office  anyone with any information about this  incident is asked to call nlvpd at  702-633  -911  or call Crime Stoppers  at this time there is no further  information available on the update of  this incident both adults still remain  in the hospital  North Las Vegas PD would like to take  this time to remind all residents that  the dangers of impaired driving and the  need to follow posted speed limit signs  and the use of proper safety restraints  this is a call to action  about DUI speed and proper child  restraints  nlvpd urges parents caregivers and  anyone traveling with children to  protect them by making sure that each  child is secure in the correct car seat  for their age height and weight  as you can see we have car seats on  display  we want to remind the public of the  dangers of driving while impaired  driving after drinking is deadly  yet it still continues to happen across  the United States if you drive while  impaired you could get arrested or Worse  be involved in a traffic collision that  causes Serious injury or death to either  yourself or others  today is a somber day as we already are  honoring the member of  Cameron Ulrich the grandson of two North  Las Vegas locals who passed away on this  day due to being hit by a car in 2018.  now we have this weekend tragedy to look  at the lives of two young children and  seriously injured that seriously injured  two women  these tragedies remind us that we need  to practice Road Safety today and every  day to keep our streets and children  safe  with the holidays coming up everyone  needs to stay vigilant and practice  responsible behaviors  please be safe ride home before plan  your ride before you start the party  choose to a non-drinker who may be a  friend that is a designated driver  if someone you know has been drinking do  not let them get behind the wheel  if you drink do not get behind the wheel  call Rideshare call a taxi there are so  many options these things are very  avoidable  and always wear your seat belt it is the  best defense against impaired drivers  the city of North Las Vegas takes all  traffic accidents seriously the health  and safety of all residents is a top  priority  though the efforts of our grant  Administration office the city was  recently awarded with additional funds  by the Nevada Department of Public  Safety  these monies will help fund initiatives  including and addressing  DUIs and reckless driving which  collaborates with other law enforcement  agencies  it does also help with increased  presence of officers at busy pedestrian  intersections crosswalks in areas of  need to decrease fatalities  funds to support dedicated staff in time  and programming to address speeding  violations enhanced informants of safety  and child safety seat laws and to reduce  distracted driving and impaired driving  we currently have displays of child  safety seats that people need to be  aware of  a regular car seat is not to be used for  a child  this is very avoidable  at this time  any questions that you may have can be  addressed to the email address of pdpio  at cityofnorthlasvegas.com  after this we will be taking a car seat  demo downstairs for everyone to see the  proper installment of a car seat  thank you very much
 

